        "content": "# Technical Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n**Status**: Draft\n**Created**: 2026-03-14\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nThe YAML Validator Command is a hand-written, dependency-free YAML syntax validator implemented as a Bun/TypeScript CLI utility. It validates YAML files for structural correctness using a line-by-line state-tracking parser and reports human-readable errors with line numbers. The design follows the project's existing patterns: pure-function modules in `src/`, kebab-case files, co-located tests, and zero external dependencies.\n\n### High-Level Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    CLI[\"CLI Entry Point<br/>validate-yaml.ts\"] -->|file path / stdin| Reader[\"File Reader<br/>(Bun.file API)\"]\n    Reader -->|raw text| Validator[\"YAML Validator<br/>yaml-validator.ts\"]\n    Validator -->|line analysis| Tokenizer[\"Line Tokenizer\"]\n    Validator -->|context tracking| StateTracker[\"State Tracker\"]\n    Validator -->|key tracking| DuplicateDetector[\"Duplicate Key<br/>Detector\"]\n    Validator -->|ValidationResult| CLI\n    CLI -->|exit code + message| Output[\"stdout / stderr\"]\n```\n\n## 2. Architecture\n\n### Component Responsibilities\n\n| Component | File | Responsibility |\n|-----------|------|----------------|\n| Types | `src/yaml-validator-types.ts` | Shared type definitions, error types, result types, enums |\n| Validator Core | `src/yaml-validator.ts` | YAML parsing and validation logic: tokenization, state tracking, error detection |\n| CLI Entry | `src/validate-yaml.ts` | Argument parsing, file reading, output formatting, exit code management |\n| Tests | `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` | Unit tests for validator core functions |\n\n### Component Interaction\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant CLI as validate-yaml.ts\n    participant Val as yaml-validator.ts\n    participant FS as Bun.file()\n\n    User->>CLI: bun run validate-yaml <file>\n    CLI->>CLI: parseArgs(process.argv)\n    alt --help or no args\n        CLI->>User: Usage text (stderr), exit 2\n    end\n    CLI->>FS: Bun.file(filePath).text()\n    alt File not found / read error\n        CLI->>User: Error message (stderr), exit 2\n    end\n    FS->>CLI: raw YAML string\n    CLI->>Val: validateYaml(content, filePath)\n    Val->>Val: splitLines()\n    loop Each line\n        Val->>Val: classifyLine(line)\n        Val->>Val: checkIndentation(line, context)\n        Val->>Val: checkQuotes(line, context)\n        Val->>Val: checkDuplicateKeys(line, context)\n        Val->>Val: updateState(lineType, context)\n    end\n    Val->>CLI: ValidationResult\n    alt Valid\n        CLI->>User: Success message (stdout), exit 0\n    else Invalid\n        CLI->>User: Error details (stderr), exit 1\n    end\n```\n\n## 3. Detailed Design\n\n### 3.1 Type Definitions (`src/yaml-validator-types.ts`)\n\n```typescript\n/** Classification of a single YAML line */\nexport enum LineType {\n  Blank = \"blank\",\n  Comment = \"comment\",\n  DocumentStart = \"document_start\",    // ---\n  DocumentEnd = \"document_end\",        // ...\n  MappingPair = \"mapping_pair\",        // key: value\n  SequenceItem = \"sequence_item\",      // - value\n  ScalarContinuation = \"scalar_continuation\",\n  Directive = \"directive\",             // %YAML etc\n}\n\n/** A single validation error */\nexport interface ValidationError {\n  line: number;        // 1-based line number\n  column?: number;     // 1-based column, if applicable\n  message: string;     // Human-readable description\n  severity: \"error\" | \"warning\";\n}\n\n/** Result of validating a YAML document */\nexport interface ValidationResult {\n  valid: boolean;\n  errors: ValidationError[];\n  documentCount: number;\n}\n\n/** Parser context state tracked across lines */\nexport interface ParserContext {\n  lineNumber: number;\n  indentStack: number[];          // Stack of indentation levels\n  inQuotedString: boolean;        // Tracking multi-line quoted strings\n  quoteChar: string | null;       // ' or \"\n  quoteStartLine: number;         // Where the quote opened\n  currentKeys: Map<string, number>[]; // Stack of key->lineNumber maps per indent level\n  documentCount: number;\n  lastLineType: LineType | null;\n  lastIndent: number;\n}\n```\n\n### 3.2 Validator Core (`src/yaml-validator.ts`)\n\nThe validator uses a **line-by-line state-tracking approach**. This is preferred over a recursive descent parser because:\n- We only need validation, not data extraction or AST construction.\n- Line-by-line processing maps naturally to line-number error reporting.\n- Simpler to implement correctly for the scoped subset of YAML 1.2.\n\n**Key Algorithms:**\n\n#### Line Classification\n\nEach non-blank, non-comment line is classified by pattern matching:\n\n```\n/^---\\s*$/         -> DocumentStart\n/^\\.\\.\\.\\s*$/      -> DocumentEnd\n/^(\\s*)-\\s/        -> SequenceItem\n/^(\\s*)([^:]+):\\s/ -> MappingPair (key extraction)\n/^(\\s*)([^:]+):$/  -> MappingPair (key only, null value)\n```\n\nThe classifier first strips comments (respecting quoted strings) and then applies pattern matching.\n\n#### Indentation Validation\n\nUses a stack-based approach:\n\n1. On each non-blank, non-comment line, compute the leading space count.\n2. **Tab check**: If the line starts with or contains leading tab characters, emit an error immediately.\n3. Compare current indent to the top of the indent stack:\n   - **Same level**: Valid sibling. Continue.\n   - **Deeper**: Valid nesting. Push new level onto stack.\n   - **Shallower**: Pop stack until matching level found. If no match, emit inconsistent indentation error.\n4. After a document separator (`---`), reset the indent stack.\n\n#### Quote Tracking\n\n1. Scan each line for unescaped quote characters (`'` or `\"`).\n2. Track open/close state across lines.\n3. If end-of-file is reached with an open quote, emit \"unclosed quoted string\" error referencing the opening line.\n4. Within a quoted string, skip all other validation (the content is opaque).\n\n#### Duplicate Key Detection\n\n1. Maintain a stack of `Map<string, number>` objects, one per indentation level.\n2. When a mapping pair is found, extract the key string.\n3. Look up the key in the current level's map:\n   - If found: Emit \"duplicate key\" error, referencing both the current and original line numbers.\n   - If not found: Insert key with current line number.\n4. When indentation decreases (popping the indent stack), discard the corresponding key maps.\n\n#### Multi-Document Handling\n\n1. `---` resets parser context (indent stack, key maps) but preserves document count and cumulative errors.\n2. `...` marks document end; subsequent content must begin with `---` or be blank/comments.\n\n### 3.3 CLI Entry Point (`src/validate-yaml.ts`)\n\n```\nArgument Parsing Logic:\n  argv[2] === undefined || argv[2] === \"--help\"  ->  print usage, exit 2\n  argv[2] === \"-\"                                 ->  read from stdin (Could Have)\n  otherwise                                       ->  treat as file path\n\nFile Reading:\n  const file = Bun.file(filePath);\n  if (!(await file.exists())) -> error, exit 2\n  const content = await file.text();\n\nOutput Formatting:\n  Valid:   stdout: \"{filePath}: Valid YAML ({N} document(s))\"\n  Invalid: stderr: \"{filePath}: Invalid YAML\\n\" + errors formatted as:\n           \"  line {N}: {message}\"\n```\n\n### 3.4 Stdin Support (Could Have)\n\nWhen the argument is `-`, read from stdin using:\n```typescript\nconst content = await Bun.stdin.text();\n```\n\nApply the same validation pipeline. Use `\"<stdin>\"` as the file name in output messages.\n\n## 4. Technology Stack\n\n| Category | Choice | Rationale |\n|----------|--------|-----------|\n| Runtime | Bun | Existing project runtime |\n| Language | TypeScript (strict mode) | Existing project language |\n| Module System | ESM (`import`/`export`) | Existing project pattern |\n| File I/O | `Bun.file()` API | Bun built-in, no dependencies |\n| Stdin I/O | `Bun.stdin.text()` | Bun built-in, no dependencies |\n| Testing | `bun:test` | Existing project test runner |\n| YAML Parsing | Hand-written line-by-line parser | Zero-dependency constraint (REQ-004) |\n\n**No new dependencies are introduced.** All logic uses Bun built-in APIs and TypeScript standard library.\n\n## 5. Implementation Plan\n\n| ID | Component | Description | Files |\n|----|-----------|-------------|-------|\n| T1 | Type Definitions | Shared types, enums, interfaces for validation errors, results, parser context | `src/yaml-validator-types.ts` |\n| T2 | Validator Core | Line classifier, indentation validator, quote tracker, duplicate key detector, main `validateYaml()` function | `src/yaml-validator.ts` |\n| T3 | CLI Entry Point | Argument parsing, file reading, output formatting, exit code management, help text | `src/validate-yaml.ts` |\n| T4 | Unit Tests | Tests for classifier, indentation, quotes, duplicates, full validation scenarios (valid + invalid YAML) | `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` |\n| T5 | Package Config | Add `validate-yaml` script to `package.json` | `package.json` |\n\n## 6. Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [T1] - Foundation types with no dependencies\n2. [T2] - Validator core depends on types from T1\n3. [T3, T4] - CLI entry and unit tests both depend on T2, independent of each other\n4. [T5] - Package.json update references T3 script path\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- T2 -> T1 (interface dependency: validator imports types)\n- T3 -> T2 (interface dependency: CLI imports validateYaml function)\n- T4 -> T2 (interface dependency: tests import validator functions)\n- T5 -> T3 (path dependency: script entry references validate-yaml.ts)\n\n**Critical Path**: T1 -> T2 -> T3 -> T5\n\n## 7. Testing Strategy\n\n### Test Value Assessment\n\n| Valuable (design for) | Avoid (do NOT design for) |\n|-----------------------|--------------------------|\n| Line classification logic (app-specific parser) | Bun.file() read behavior |\n| Indentation validation algorithm | TypeScript Map behavior |\n| Quote tracking state machine | process.argv parsing mechanics |\n| Duplicate key detection | Console output formatting |\n| End-to-end valid/invalid YAML scenarios | Bun.stdin API behavior |\n| Exit code correctness | File system permission edge cases |\n| Error message content (line numbers, descriptions) | - |\n\n### Test Categories\n\n#### Unit Tests (`src/yaml-validator.test.ts`)\n\n**Line Classification Tests:**\n- Blank lines, comment lines, document separators\n- Mapping pairs with various value types\n- Sequence items with various value types\n- Edge cases: colons in values, hashes in strings\n\n**Indentation Validation Tests:**\n- Correct nested indentation (2-space, 4-space)\n- Tab character detection\n- Inconsistent indentation detection\n- Indentation reset after document separator\n\n**Quote Tracking Tests:**\n- Balanced single quotes\n- Balanced double quotes\n- Unclosed quote detection with correct line reference\n- Escaped quotes within strings\n- Colons and hashes inside quoted strings (should not trigger other errors)\n\n**Duplicate Key Detection Tests:**\n- Unique keys at same level (valid)\n- Duplicate keys at same level (invalid)\n- Same key at different nesting levels (valid)\n- Duplicate key detection after document separator reset\n\n**Full Validation Integration Tests:**\n- Valid: Simple key-value file\n- Valid: Nested mappings with sequences\n- Valid: Multi-document file\n- Valid: File with comments only\n- Valid: Mixed scalars (strings, numbers, booleans, null)\n- Invalid: Tabs for indentation\n- Invalid: Unclosed quoted string\n- Invalid: Duplicate keys\n- Invalid: Inconsistent indentation\n- Invalid: Malformed mapping (missing colon separator)\n\n**Error Reporting Tests:**\n- Correct line numbers in error output\n- Meaningful error descriptions\n- Multiple errors detected in single file\n\n### Test Execution\n\nAll tests run via `bun test`, consistent with existing project pattern. Tests are co-located as `src/yaml-validator.test.ts`.\n\n## 8. Deployment Design\n\nNo separate deployment is required. The feature is delivered as source files within the existing project structure.\n\n**Integration steps:**\n1. New source files added to `src/` directory.\n2. New `validate-yaml` script added to `package.json`.\n3. Command is immediately available via `bun run validate-yaml <file>` or `bun run src/validate-yaml.ts <file>`.\n\n**Rollback:** Remove the added files and the script entry from `package.json`. No other project files are modified.\n\n## 9. Documentation Impact\n\n| Type | Target | Section | KB Source | Rationale |\n|------|--------|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| edit | `.rp1/context/modules.md` | Modules | modules.md | Add yaml-validator-types, yaml-validator, validate-yaml module entries |\n| edit | `.rp1/context/architecture.md` | Scripts | architecture.md | Add validate-yaml script to Scripts section |\n| edit | `.rp1/context/index.md` | Project Structure | index.md | Add new files to structure listing |\n\n## 10. Design Decisions Log\n\n| ID | Decision | Choice | Rationale | Alternatives Considered |\n|----|----------|--------|-----------|------------------------|\n| D1 | Parser approach | Line-by-line state tracker | Validation-only use case; maps naturally to line-number reporting; simpler than recursive descent for the scoped YAML subset | Recursive descent parser (more complex, builds AST we don't need); Regex-only (too fragile for nested structures) |\n| D2 | Module decomposition | 3 modules (types, validator, CLI) | Separates concerns: types are shared, validator is testable pure logic, CLI handles I/O side effects | Single file (too large, harder to test); More granular split (over-engineering for this scope) |\n| D3 | Error accumulation vs. fail-fast | Accumulate all errors | Users benefit from seeing all problems at once rather than fixing one at a time | Fail-fast on first error (simpler but worse UX) |\n| D4 | Indentation tracking | Stack-based | Natural fit for YAML's nesting model; efficient O(depth) space | Counter-based (cannot detect inconsistencies); Regex-only (too fragile) |\n| D5 | Duplicate key scope | Per-indentation-level with reset on dedent | Matches YAML spec semantics where duplicate keys are only prohibited at the same mapping level | Global key tracking (incorrect -- same key at different levels is valid); No duplicate detection (misses REQ-007) |\n| D6 | CLI argument style | Positional argument (file path) | Matches existing project pattern (src/index.ts uses process.argv[2]); simple and conventional | Flag-based (--file, --input) -- over-engineered for single-purpose command |\n| D7 | Exit code scheme | 0/1/2 | Standard Unix convention, explicitly required by REQ-005 | 0/1 only (loses distinction between invalid YAML and operational error) |\n| D8 | Stdin support | Include as secondary input mode | Low additional complexity; high utility for CI pipes (REQ-009) | Omit (loses pipe integration capability) |\n"
