        "content": "# Development Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n**Feature ID**: yaml-validator-command\n**Status**: Not Started\n**Progress**: 0% (0 of 8 tasks)\n**Estimated Effort**: 3 days\n**Started**: 2026-03-14\n\n## Overview\n\nA dependency-free YAML syntax validator implemented as a Bun/TypeScript CLI utility. It validates YAML files for structural correctness using a line-by-line state-tracking parser and reports human-readable errors with line numbers. The implementation follows the project's existing patterns: pure-function modules in `src/`, kebab-case files, co-located tests, and zero external dependencies.\n\n## Implementation DAG\n\n**Parallel Groups** (tasks with no inter-dependencies):\n\n1. [I1] - Foundation types with no dependencies\n2. [I2] - Validator core depends on types from I1\n3. [I3, I4] - CLI entry and unit tests both depend on I2, independent of each other\n4. [I5] - Package.json update references I3 script path\n\n**Dependencies**:\n\n- I2 -> I1 (interface dependency: validator imports types)\n- I3 -> I2 (interface dependency: CLI imports validateYaml function)\n- I4 -> I2 (interface dependency: tests import validator functions)\n- I5 -> I3 (path dependency: script entry references validate-yaml.ts)\n\n**Critical Path**: I1 -> I2 -> I3 -> I5\n\n## Task Breakdown\n\n### Phase 1: Foundation Types\n\n- [ ] **I1**: Implement shared type definitions for the YAML validator `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#31-type-definitions](design.md#31-type-definitions)\n\n    **Effort**: 1 hour\n\n    **Dependencies**: None\n\n    **Files**: `src/yaml-validator-types.ts`\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `LineType` enum is defined with all variants: Blank, Comment, DocumentStart, DocumentEnd, MappingPair, SequenceItem, ScalarContinuation, Directive\n    - [ ] `ValidationError` interface is defined with `line` (number), `column` (optional number), `message` (string), and `severity` (\"error\" | \"warning\") fields\n    - [ ] `ValidationResult` interface is defined with `valid` (boolean), `errors` (ValidationError[]), and `documentCount` (number) fields\n    - [ ] `ParserContext` interface is defined with `lineNumber`, `indentStack`, `inQuotedString`, `quoteChar`, `quoteStartLine`, `currentKeys`, `documentCount`, `lastLineType`, and `lastIndent` fields\n    - [ ] File uses ESM export syntax and compiles under TypeScript strict mode\n    - [ ] File follows kebab-case naming convention\n\n### Phase 2: Validator Core\n\n- [ ] **I2**: Implement the YAML validator core with line-by-line state-tracking parser `[complexity:complex]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#32-validator-core](design.md#32-validator-core)\n\n    **Effort**: 8 hours\n\n    **Dependencies**: I1\n\n    **Files**: `src/yaml-validator.ts`\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `classifyLine()` function correctly identifies all `LineType` variants using the documented regex patterns (DocumentStart, DocumentEnd, SequenceItem, MappingPair, Blank, Comment, Directive)\n    - [ ] `classifyLine()` strips comments while respecting quoted strings before pattern matching\n    - [ ] Stack-based indentation validation detects tab characters and emits errors immediately\n    - [ ] Indentation validation correctly handles sibling (same level), nesting (deeper), and dedent (shallower) cases\n    - [ ] Indentation validation emits \"inconsistent indentation\" error when dedent level does not match any level on the stack\n    - [ ] Indent stack resets after `---` document separator\n    - [ ] Quote tracking correctly tracks open/close state for both single and double quotes across lines\n    - [ ] Quote tracking emits \"unclosed quoted string\" error at EOF referencing the opening line number\n    - [ ] Content inside quoted strings is skipped for other validation checks\n    - [ ] Duplicate key detection maintains per-indentation-level key maps and emits errors when a duplicate key is found at the same mapping level, referencing both original and duplicate line numbers\n    - [ ] Key maps are discarded when indentation decreases (dedent)\n    - [ ] Multi-document handling: `---` resets parser context (indent stack, key maps) while preserving document count and cumulative errors\n    - [ ] `...` document end marker is handled: subsequent non-blank/non-comment content without `---` triggers an error\n    - [ ] Main `validateYaml(content, filePath)` function returns a complete `ValidationResult` with accumulated errors and document count\n    - [ ] All errors include accurate 1-based line numbers\n    - [ ] Multiple errors are accumulated in a single validation pass (not fail-fast)\n    - [ ] No external dependencies are imported; only Bun built-ins and TypeScript standard library are used\n\n### Phase 3: CLI and Tests (Parallel)\n\n- [ ] **I3**: Implement the CLI entry point with argument parsing, file reading, and output formatting `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#33-cli-entry-point](design.md#33-cli-entry-point)\n\n    **Effort**: 4 hours\n\n    **Dependencies**: I2\n\n    **Files**: `src/validate-yaml.ts`\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Running with no arguments prints usage instructions to stderr and exits with code 2\n    - [ ] Running with `--help` prints usage instructions to stderr and exits with code 2\n    - [ ] Running with a valid file path reads the file using `Bun.file()` API and passes content to `validateYaml()`\n    - [ ] Running with a non-existent file path prints a clear error message to stderr and exits with code 2\n    - [ ] Valid YAML produces a success message on stdout containing the file path, the word \"Valid\", and the document count, then exits with code 0\n    - [ ] Invalid YAML produces error details on stderr formatted as `\"  line {N}: {message}\"` for each error, then exits with code 1\n    - [ ] Running with `-` as argument reads from stdin via `Bun.stdin.text()` and uses `\"<stdin>\"` as the file name in output\n    - [ ] Exit codes follow the documented scheme: 0 (valid), 1 (invalid YAML), 2 (operational error)\n    - [ ] File uses ESM imports and compiles under TypeScript strict mode\n\n- [ ] **I4**: Implement comprehensive unit tests for the YAML validator `[complexity:medium]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#7-testing-strategy](design.md#7-testing-strategy)\n\n    **Effort**: 6 hours\n\n    **Dependencies**: I2\n\n    **Files**: `src/yaml-validator.test.ts`\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] Line classification tests cover: blank lines, comment lines, document separators (`---`, `...`), mapping pairs with various value types, sequence items, edge cases (colons in values, hashes in strings)\n    - [ ] Indentation validation tests cover: correct nested indentation (2-space, 4-space), tab character detection, inconsistent indentation detection, indentation reset after document separator\n    - [ ] Quote tracking tests cover: balanced single quotes, balanced double quotes, unclosed quote detection with correct line reference, escaped quotes, colons and hashes inside quoted strings not triggering false errors\n    - [ ] Duplicate key detection tests cover: unique keys at same level (valid), duplicate keys at same level (invalid), same key at different nesting levels (valid), duplicate detection reset after document separator\n    - [ ] Full validation integration tests cover valid scenarios: simple key-value, nested mappings with sequences, multi-document, comments only, mixed scalar types\n    - [ ] Full validation integration tests cover invalid scenarios: tabs for indentation, unclosed quoted string, duplicate keys, inconsistent indentation\n    - [ ] Error reporting tests verify: correct line numbers, meaningful descriptions, multiple errors detected in single file\n    - [ ] All tests use `bun:test` runner and are co-located in `src/`\n    - [ ] Tests pass when run via `bun test`\n\n### Phase 4: Package Integration\n\n- [ ] **I5**: Add validate-yaml script entry to package.json `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#8-deployment-design](design.md#8-deployment-design)\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Dependencies**: I3\n\n    **Files**: `package.json`\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] A `\"validate-yaml\"` script entry exists in `package.json` `\"scripts\"` section pointing to `src/validate-yaml.ts`\n    - [ ] Running `bun run validate-yaml <file>` works identically to `bun run src/validate-yaml.ts <file>`\n    - [ ] No new entries are added to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`\n    - [ ] `devDependencies` contains only the pre-existing `@types/bun` entry\n\n### Documentation\n\n- [ ] **D1**: Update modules.md with YAML validator module entries `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#9-documentation-impact](design.md#9-documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: `.rp1/context/modules.md`\n\n    **Section**: Modules\n\n    **KB Source**: modules.md\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Dependencies**: I2, I3\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `yaml-validator-types` module entry added with description of shared types, enums, and interfaces\n    - [ ] `yaml-validator` module entry added with description of validation logic and key exported functions (`validateYaml`, `classifyLine`)\n    - [ ] `validate-yaml` module entry added with description of CLI entry point and argument handling\n    - [ ] Entries follow the existing format and conventions in modules.md\n\n- [ ] **D2**: Update architecture.md with validate-yaml script reference `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#9-documentation-impact](design.md#9-documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: `.rp1/context/architecture.md`\n\n    **Section**: Scripts\n\n    **KB Source**: architecture.md\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Dependencies**: I5\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `validate-yaml` script added to the Scripts section with description, invocation syntax, and exit code semantics\n    - [ ] Entry follows the existing format and conventions in architecture.md\n\n- [ ] **D3**: Update index.md with new source files in project structure `[complexity:simple]`\n\n    **Reference**: [design.md#9-documentation-impact](design.md#9-documentation-impact)\n\n    **Type**: edit\n\n    **Target**: `.rp1/context/index.md`\n\n    **Section**: Project Structure\n\n    **KB Source**: index.md\n\n    **Effort**: 30 minutes\n\n    **Dependencies**: I1, I2, I3, I4\n\n    **Acceptance Criteria**:\n\n    - [ ] `src/yaml-validator-types.ts` added to the project structure listing\n    - [ ] `src/yaml-validator.ts` added to the project structure listing\n    - [ ] `src/validate-yaml.ts` added to the project structure listing\n    - [ ] `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` added to the project structure listing\n    - [ ] Entries follow the existing format and conventions in index.md\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n\n### REQ-001: File Path Input\n- [ ] AC-001a: Running the command with a valid file path reads and validates that file\n- [ ] AC-001b: Running the command with a non-existent file path outputs a clear error message and exits with a non-zero code\n- [ ] AC-001c: Running the command with no arguments outputs usage instructions to stderr and exits with a non-zero code\n\n### REQ-002: Valid YAML Reporting\n- [ ] AC-002a: A valid YAML file produces a message containing the word \"valid\" (case-insensitive) on stdout\n- [ ] AC-002b: The process exit code is 0\n\n### REQ-003: Invalid YAML Error Reporting\n- [ ] AC-003a: An invalid YAML file produces an error message on stderr containing a line number\n- [ ] AC-003b: The error message includes a human-readable description of the syntax problem\n- [ ] AC-003c: The process exit code is non-zero (1 for validation failure)\n\n### REQ-004: Zero New Dependencies\n- [ ] AC-004a: After implementation, `package.json` `dependencies` remains absent or empty\n- [ ] AC-004b: After implementation, `package.json` `devDependencies` contains only `@types/bun`\n- [ ] AC-004c: No `node_modules` additions beyond what Bun provides natively\n\n### REQ-005: Exit Code Semantics\n- [ ] AC-005a: Exit code 0 when input YAML is valid\n- [ ] AC-005b: Exit code 1 when input YAML has syntax errors\n- [ ] AC-005c: Exit code 2 when the file cannot be read or other operational error occurs\n\n### REQ-006: Basic YAML Syntax Coverage\n- [ ] AC-006a: A file with nested key-value mappings is accepted as valid\n- [ ] AC-006b: A file with list items using `-` prefix is accepted as valid\n- [ ] AC-006c: A file with single-quoted and double-quoted strings is accepted as valid\n- [ ] AC-006d: A file containing only comments is accepted as valid\n- [ ] AC-006e: A file with `---` document separators is accepted as valid\n\n### REQ-007: Common Error Detection\n- [ ] AC-007a: A file using tabs for indentation is reported as invalid with a message mentioning tabs\n- [ ] AC-007b: A file with inconsistent indentation is reported as invalid\n- [ ] AC-007c: A file with an unclosed quoted string is reported as invalid\n- [ ] AC-007d: A file with duplicate keys at the same level is reported as invalid or warned\n\n### REQ-008: Command Integration\n- [ ] AC-008a: A `validate-yaml` script entry exists in `package.json` `scripts`\n- [ ] AC-008b: Running the script with a file argument works identically to direct invocation\n\n### REQ-009: Standard Input Support\n- [ ] AC-009a: Piping YAML content to the command with `-` as the argument validates the piped content\n- [ ] AC-009b: The same success/failure output and exit code conventions apply to stdin input\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] All implementation tasks (I1-I5) completed\n- [ ] All unit tests passing via `bun test`\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria verified\n- [ ] Documentation tasks (D1-D3) completed\n- [ ] Code reviewed\n- [ ] No new external dependencies added to package.json\n- [ ] All files follow project conventions (kebab-case files,